# Frontend

Plain JavaScript and Svelte 5 runes. No TypeScript, no SvelteKit, no router library.

- Call the backend only through `frontend/src/lib/api.js`. The browser never reads CSV or markdown.
- Add routes in `matchRoute` (`router.svelte.js`) and the branch in `App.svelte`. Links are `<a href="/...">`; `router.handleClick` intercepts plain left-clicks. nginx already serves `index.html` for every path.
- Module state lives in `app.svelte.js` (toasts, banner, pull) and `jobsCache.svelte.js`. Reload a page when `pull.finishedCount` changes.
- Use `$state`, `$derived`, and `$effect`. Handlers are `onclick` / `onkeydown`, not `on:click`.
- Style with component `<style>` and the tokens in `app.css` (`--accent`, `--good`, `--bad`, `--warn`). Keep 14px body text and 20px `h1`.
- Inbox keys `S` `A` `D` `J` `K`, the arrows, and `Z` stay inactive while an input, textarea, select, or contenteditable is focused.
- Failures go through `reportError`. A status change the user can reverse uses a toast `undo` that calls `api.deleteEvent`.
- Pure filter, sort, and date logic goes in `frontend/src/lib/`.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<button on:click={save}>Save</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<button onclick={save}>Save <kbd>S</kbd></button>
```
